{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The flash drive fits my practical computer use: transferring files and keeping installation tools handy gives it a clear purpose alongside my recent accessories.",
    "The Bluetooth adapter and microSD card could extend equipment I already use, by adding wireless peripheral connectivity or storage for Raspberry Pi projects, provided compatibility checks out."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another HDMI cable or pair of headphones repeats something I already have without addressing a new need; my recent purchases make organizing and maintaining my setup feel more relevant.",
    "The smart speaker and streaming stick do not support my current computer and networking tasks, while the optical-audio and USB-C accessories depend on connection needs I have not shown."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying electronics seems to have been taken as interest in a broad range of gadgets, even when I cannot connect them to a current task.",
    "Past cable and headphone purchases seem to have been treated as reasons to buy more similar items, although those purchases may already have met my needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet accessories, headphone mount, backpack and cleaning equipment suggest I am making an existing computer setup more useful, organized and easier to maintain.",
    "The purpose and compatibility of each accessory matter: extra Raspberry Pi storage could be useful, but that does not establish Garmin compatibility or a need for USB-C accessories."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in useful computer accessories but stretched it into gadgets and repeat purchases without a clear current purpose."
}"}
